## Why This Is Asked
Tests hardware offload, OS UDP paths, and QoS interplay in a multi-region fabric, focusing on telemetry reliability under bursts with no app changes.

## Key Concepts
- NIC RSS hashing and RX queues
- UDP tail drops and sockstat counters
- VXLAN/EVPN MTU and fragmentation
- Per-tenant rate limiting and edge QoS

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple UDP burst tester (Node.js)
const dgram = require('dgram');
const client = dgram.createSocket('udp4');
const TARGET = {host: 'collector.example', port: 9000};
let sent = 0, burst = 1000;
function sendNext(){
  if (sent >= burst) { client.close(); return; }
  client.send(Buffer.from('x'), 0, 1, TARGET.port, TARGET.host, () => {});
  sent++;
  if (sent % 10 === 0) setImmediate(sendNext);
  else setTimeout(sendNext, 0);
}
sendNext();
```

